=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, fibroblast TE ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.00701
  lasso keeps 49 of 61 codons; sets 12 to exactly 0: TTT, TTG, TGT, CTT, CCT, CCA, CAG, AAA, GTA, GCA, GAA, GAG
  of those 12, 0 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 0 nominally significant codons overall, 0 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9903, Spearman rho = 0.9913; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.882 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS +37.513 / 5.401, lasso -0.175 / 4.798
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS -39.4334, lasso -1.8096

